DeepSeek + DuckDuckGo MCP wiring

This project exposes a web_search tool to DeepSeek. The server bridges that tool into DuckDuckGo MCP first, then Context7 MCP, then fallback web search if needed.

How the tool call works (DeepSeek side)
- DeepSeek uses Chat Completions with tools (function calling). The model returns tool_calls with function.name + JSON arguments.
- The server executes the tool and sends the tool result back to DeepSeek, then DeepSeek continues.

DuckDuckGo MCP details
- MCP Streamable HTTP endpoint: http://HOST:8020/mcp
- Tool name: web-search
- Args: query (string, required), numResults (integer, optional), page (integer, optional), mode (short|detailed, optional)
- API key: not required for DuckDuckGo MCP

Context7 MCP details
- MCP Streamable HTTP endpoint: http://HOST:8010/mcp
- Tool name: resolve-library-id (first) then query-docs
- Args: resolve-library-id needs query + libraryName; query-docs needs libraryId + query

Environment wiring (this repo)
- MCP_DDG_URL=http://HOST:8020/mcp
- MCP_DDG_TOOL=web-search
- MCP_DDG_QUERY_KEY=query
- MCP_DDG_RESULTS_KEY=numResults
- MCP_CTX7_URL=http://HOST:8010/mcp
- MCP_CTX7_TOOL=resolve-library-id
- MCP_CTX7_QUERY_KEY=libraryName
- MCP_CTX7_RESULTS_KEY=disabled

Host vs Docker
- If the API runs on your host (npm run dev), use 127.0.0.1 for HOST.
- If the API runs in Docker Compose, use service names (duckduckgo-mcp, context7-mcp).

Quick manual test (optional)
- POST initialize, tools/list, then tools/call to http://HOST:8020/mcp
- Example call payload for web-search:
  {"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"method":"tools/call","params":{"name":"web-search","arguments":{"query":"Bun runtime","numResults":3}}}

UI behavior
- For user search requests and news queries, the server runs DuckDuckGo MCP first.
- The UI should display "ducking..." when DuckDuckGo MCP is attempted.
- Terminal tools are only allowed for news if fewer than 3 sources are found.
